1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,296
My mother is going to drop the coffee mug at exactly seven-fourteen.

2
00:00:04,596 --> 00:00:11,316
She has done it ten thousand times. Today is no different. The ceramic shatters on the tile.

3
00:00:11,616 --> 00:00:19,200
I catch the falling pieces before they hit the floor. She freezes, her mouth open in a silent scream.

4
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:26,556
Time is broken. The clock on the wall stopped at seven-fourteen. Again. I am trapped in today.

5
00:00:26,856 --> 00:00:35,040
Then, the front door unlocks. Someone walks in who has never, in ten thousand days, been here.

6
00:00:35,340 --> 00:00:41,652
An old man walks through the door, holding the exact same red coffee mug, completely whole.

7
00:00:41,952 --> 00:00:49,056
He looks at me, tears in his eyes. He says, You finally noticed the pattern, son.

8
00:00:49,356 --> 00:00:55,548
I look back at my mother, who is still frozen like a statue. But her eyes are blinking.

9
00:00:55,848 --> 00:01:04,080
She isn't part of the loop. She's the warden. And today, she finally let the old man out.

10
00:01:04,380 --> 00:01:10,212
If today is the first new day in years... who was living all the days before?
